# .gitattributes
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS, and it is narrower than it looks.
#
# Two gates, `spine-css-fresh` and `glyphs-fresh`, decide whether a generated
# file is current by comparing it BYTE FOR BYTE against the string the
# generator would write:
#
#     if (current !== next) { ...STALE... }
#
# The generators write LF. On Windows, git's autocrlf rewrites the working tree
# to CRLF the next time it touches the file. The content is then identical and
# the bytes are not, so the gate reports the React kit is rendering an older
# design than the mockups show, when it is rendering exactly the same design.
#
# That happened on 2026-08-07. Both files were regenerated and `git diff` came
# back completely empty, which is the proof: nothing was stale, the comparison
# was.
#
# Pinning these two to LF makes the byte comparison mean what it says. It is
# not a repo-wide line-ending policy and it deliberately does not touch any
# other file: the rest of the tree can keep whatever git decides, because
# nothing else in it is verified by byte equality against a generator.

src/styles/atlas-spine.css      text eol=lf
src/components/spine2/glyphs.ts text eol=lf
